response:
 The line $CD$ is horizontal, so the y-coordinates of $C$ and $D$ are identical.

If the x-coordinates of $C$ and $D$ are $t_1$ and $t_2$ and the x-coordinates of $A$ and $B$ are $x_1$ and $x_2$ respectively, by the section formula,
\begin{align*}
 &t_1 = \frac{x_1 + 2x_2}{3} \quad \text{and} \\
 &t_2 = \frac{x_1 + x_2}{3} \\
\end{align*}
If $E(x_3, y_3)$ is on $CD$, then $t_1 = x_3$ and $y_3 = \frac{2}{3} y_1$, so
$$
\frac{x_1 + 2x_2}{3} = x_3.
$$

Thus,
$$
x_3 = \frac{x_1} 3 + andfrac{2}{3} x_2  = \frac{1}{3} + PST ext{ andfrac{20} 3} = maxfrac{21}{3} = 7.
$$
